Make the shared GL context current before rendering plate thumbnails.

GLCanvas3D::render_thumbnail never calls _set_current(). Under Wayland, WebKit
(the home page and other web views) makes GDK create its own paint GL context,
and GDK makes that context current on the main thread while drawing. When the
Preview canvas gains focus after slicing, on_set_focus ->
update_all_plate_thumbnails renders the 3D scene in GDK's context, where none of
the GLModel VAO/VBO/IBO names exist: the binds fail, glDrawElements reads the
index "pointer" as client memory at address 0, and libnvidia-eglcore segfaults.

--- a/src/slic3r/GUI/GLCanvas3D.cpp
+++ b/src/slic3r/GUI/GLCanvas3D.cpp
@@ -2248,6 +2248,12 @@
                                   bool                      for_picking,
                                   bool                      ban_light)
 {
+    // The shared context is not guaranteed to be current here: on Wayland, GDK
+    // makes its own paint context current while drawing other widgets (e.g. the
+    // WebKit views), and this canvas's VAOs/VBOs do not exist in that context.
+    if (!_set_current())
+        return;
+
     GLShaderProgram* shader = nullptr;
     if (for_picking)
         shader = wxGetApp().get_shader("flat");
@@ -2286,6 +2292,12 @@
                                   bool                               for_picking,
                                   bool                               ban_light)
